&lt;p&gt;Hi! We’re hipages, an ASX-listed tech company and Australia’s #1 digital platform connecting households with trusted home improvement businesses. We&#39;re on a mission to transform the home improvement industry to build better lives for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With teams across Australia, New Zealand, the Philippines and Vietnam, we work as one team with a shared purpose. We’re proud to be a certified &lt;strong&gt;Great Place to Work&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;WORK180’s #1 Employer for Women&lt;/strong&gt;. At hipages, you’ll find real impact, career growth and a workplace where everyone belongs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re building &lt;em&gt;the&lt;/em&gt; shared platform that makes every hipages engineer, product manager and designer and every AI agent working on their behalf, faster, safer and more effective. We own the hipages agentic harness and software factory: the shared kernel (identity, audit logging, shared memory/context, a plugin/skill registry, org-wide safety limits and a behavioural baseline), cloud agents plus the encouraged per-team &quot;forks&quot; (bundled MCP servers, skills, prompts and UX surfaces).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll go beyond code generation to improve one or many parts of the whole software development lifecycle (SDLC), building AI workflows that are contextually aware of our codebase and conventions, integrated into how engineers already work, and continuously improving. This is platform-engineering-shaped work: you&#39;ll build new platforms, treat fellow engineers, product managers and designers as your customers, and care equally about developer experience (DX) and agent experience (AX).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is one of the highest leverage pieces of work in the organisation, and will shape how hipages continues to build awesome software that households, home services businesses and our internal teams love to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why join our Engineering team?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary, benefits, and everyday discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house Talent Development team to prioritise personal and career growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on learning opportunities and workshops for continuous upskilling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you will add value:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, ship, and maintain harness and platform features: plugins, skills, MCP integrations, internal AI-enabled CLIs, and scaffolding, with guidance from more experienced engineers, ensuring everything you build is robust, tested, and observable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve hipages’ development experience across the SDLC, through better tooling, higher test coverage and cleaner code and data structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wire up agent tooling: tool-use, scoped permissions, error handling and automated verification via Playwright and Maestro and instrument behaviour in Honeycomb.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot complex AI tooling issues across both platform and product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with version control and CI/CD, safely rolling changes forward and back, and contribute to production infrastructure on AWS/Kubernetes with Terraform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate AI outputs for correctness and appropriateness before adoption, and share useful AI use cases and learnings with your peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on use of agentic coding tools (Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot or similar), with eagerness to go deep on LLMs, AI agents, MCP and prompt engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building MCP servers, agent skills, or other agentic integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing automated evals and tests (unit, integration and/or end-to-end)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Containerisation (Docker) and familiar with running workloads on Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD principles and practices, and confident with git-style version control (branching, reviews, rolling changes forward and back safely)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional software development experience, writing clean, tested, maintainable code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in one or more modern languages, such as TypeScript/JavaScript and/or Python preferred (but we’re pretty flexible)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and integrating APIs, and a good understanding of what makes tooling pleasant for other engineers to consume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an AWS (or comparable cloud) environment and using its core services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life at hipages:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re more than just a workplace. We’re a place where you can be yourself, do great work and grow your career. Recognised as a Great Place to Work, our inclusive, supportive culture helps people thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll use the best tools and tech, with real impact on our products and customers. We invest in your development and lead with coaching, not micromanagement – it’s why 85% of our team say their leader is great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And there’s more:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diverse, collaborative teams that love solving problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile squads, hackathons, off-sites and roadshows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra leave for birthdays, volunteering, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Healthy snacks, continental breakfast and fresh fruit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sydney CBD office near Town Hall and Gadigal Stations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored growth support, mentoring and stretch projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A vibrant social scene - we work hard and have fun doing it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prioritise Diversity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At hipages,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;innovation and collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;thrive in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;diverse and inclusive &lt;/strong&gt;teams. We don’t expect you to know everything - we care more about who you are as a person, a team member, and a leader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proud to be endorsed by&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;WORK180&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;for supporting women’s careers and we value diversity across culture, age, gender identity and sexual orientation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Research shows that men often apply when they meet just 60% of the criteria, while women and minority groups wait until they tick every box. If you think you’d be a great fit - even if you don’t meet every requirement- we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re also a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Circle Back Initiative Employer&lt;/strong&gt;, which means we commit to responding to every applicant.&lt;/p&gt;
